    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0481" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/295</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador Penfield </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 21, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1167. Your 1185, 14th. Will Ghiloni’s sworn statement be accepted? If not, what
                    guaranty will be required? Again mention that Department’s records show clearly
                    Ghiloni was impressed into Italian army and did not volunteer. This Government
                    endeavored obtain his release from Italian army but without success.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
